A dramatic satellite view of Earth from space in the style of Vincent van Gogh, featuring the Pacific Ocean with a massive swirling hurricane rendered in thick, expressive brushstrokes of deep blues, turquoise, and white. The cyclone's spiral bands twist with characteristic Van Gogh movement and energy, reminiscent of Starry Night's famous swirls. The Hawaiian islands appear as small dark shapes in the storm's path. The curvature of Earth is visible at the edges, with the atmosphere glowing in golden yellows and oranges where sunlight meets the planet's limb. Impasto technique creates texture in the churning clouds and ocean waves below.
